            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.088,
            0.595,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "13. Write 4 equations whose solution is u = 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.114,
            0.848,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "14. The Bakhśhāli Manuscript (300 CE) mentions the following problem. The amount given to the first person is not known. The second person is given twice as much as the first. The third person is given thrice as much as the second; and the fourth person four times as much as the third. The total amount distributed is 132. What is the amount given to the first person?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.242,
            0.847,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "15. The height of a giraffe is two and a half metres more than half its height. How tall is the giraffe?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.289,
            0.847,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": "16. Two separate figures are given below. Each figure shows the first few positions in a sequence of arrangements made with sticks. Identify the pattern and answer the following questions for each figure:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.353,
            0.847,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": "(a) How many squares are in position number 11 of the sequence?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.376,
            0.847,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": "(b) How many sticks are needed to make the arrangement in position number 11 of the sequence?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.42,
            0.847,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": "(c) Can an arrangement in this sequence be made using exactly 85 sticks? If yes, which position number will it correspond to?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.463,
            0.847,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "(d) Can an arrangement in this sequence be made using exactly 150 sticks? If yes, which position number will it correspond to?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.246,
            0.511,
            0.798,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_24_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.669,
            0.846,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "17. A number increased by 36 is equal to ten times itself. What is the number?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.716,
            0.41,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "18. Solve these equations:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.742,
            0.353,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": "(a) 5(r + 2) = 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.742,
            0.74,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": "(b) – 3(u + 2) = 2(u – 1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.768,
            0.369,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": "(c) 2(7 – 2n) = – 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.768,
            0.693,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "(d) 2(x – 4) = – 16"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.794,
            0.43,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": "(e) 6(x – 1) = 2(x – 1) – 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.794,
            0.692,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": "(  f  ) \\quad 3 - 7s = 7 - 3s",
          "image_source": "images/page_24_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.82,
            0.417,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": "(g) 2x + 1 = 6 – (2x – 3)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.82,
            0.807,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": "(h) 10 – 5x = 3(x – 4) – 2(x – 7)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.852,
            0.847,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "19. Solve the equations to find a path from Start to the End. Show your work in the given boxes provided and colour your path as you proceed."
